# Claude Code local session state — machine/session-specific, not shared
.claude/settings.local.json

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Word lock files (created automatically while a .docx is open)
~$*.docx

# Real client financial statements used as local test data (Projection Report,
# Sales & Purchase Book, Depreciation…). This repo is PUBLIC — client data must
# never be committed. The app's own tokenized templates are .docx and stay
# tracked; every client sample is a workbook or a generated report, so ignoring
# those two types here also covers any new sample dropped in later.
assets/templates/*.xlsx
assets/templates/*.xls
assets/templates/*.ods
assets/templates/*.csv
assets/templates/*.pdf

# Row-level database dumps: pre-migration snapshots and the client master rows
# themselves. Same reason as above — these are real client names, PANs and
# addresses. The annotated migrations in db/ stay tracked; only the data does
# not. See db/2026-07-26_client_master_reload.sql for how the two fit together.
db/backups/

# Local-only archives kept for retrievability, NOT for publication. Both carry
# real client names in file paths (the permission rules and two memory files
# reference client workbooks by name), and this repo is PUBLIC. They live on
# disk beside the tracked history so nothing is lost; they just never ship.
# See docs/history/README.md.
docs/history/settings.local.json.bak
docs/history/memory-*/

# Third-party Claude Code plugin cloned into the project root (4.2 MB, its own
# git repo, github.com/JuliusBrussee/caveman). Nothing to do with this app —
# ignored so it can never be swept into a commit by `git add .`.
caveman/

# Leftover from the removed OCR Extract module (2026-08-18). The tracked files
# in ocr_service/ are gone; what can remain on a machine that once ran the
# service is its 880 MB Python venv/ and __pycache__, which used to be ignored
# by ocr_service/.gitignore — deleted along with everything else. Ignored here
# so `git add .` can never sweep that into a commit. Safe to delete the folder.
ocr_service/
